---
source: crates/gamepadii/tests/cli.rs
expression: "help(&[])"
---
CLI (and later TUI) for GP2040-CE gamepads: status, input modes, profiles

Usage: gamepadii [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  status  The pad on USB: input mode (with a confidence), USB ids, bus and port
  info    Firmware, board, memory, input mode, profiles and boot buttons (needs web-config)
  backup  Save every readable setting to one JSON file (needs web-config)
  reboot  Restart the pad into gamepad mode, web-config or BOOTSEL (needs web-config)
  help    Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
      --format <FORMAT>
          Output format

          Possible values:
          - human:  Text for people
          - json:   The versioned JSON contract ("schema": 1)
          - waybar: One line of waybar custom-module JSON; `status` only
          
          [default: human]

      --json
          Same as `--format json`

      --host <HOST>
          Talk to the web configurator at HOST (host, host:port or http://host) without looking for the pad on USB first. The default is to find it on USB and use 192.168.7.1

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

  -V, --version
          Print version
